<exercisegroup xml:id="exercisegroup-vector-geom-dot-prod-vs-vec-add">
<title>Dot product versus addition</title>

<introduction><p>
	In each case:
	<ol>

		<li xml:id="instruction-exercisegroup-vector-geom-dot-prod-vs-vec-add-first-add">
			Compute <m> \uvec{u} + \uvec{v} </m>,
			then use that result to compute <m> \dotprod{(\uvec{u} + \uvec{v})}{\uvec{w}} </m>.
		</li>

		<li xml:id="instruction-exercisegroup-vector-geom-dot-prod-vs-vec-add-first-dot-prod">
			Separately compute <m> \udotprod{u}{w} </m> and <m> \udotprod{v}{w} </m>,
			then use those results to compute <m> \udotprod{u}{w} + \udotprod{v}{w} </m>.
		</li>

		<li>
			Compare your results
			in <xref ref="instruction-exercisegroup-vector-geom-dot-prod-vs-vec-add-first-add">part</xref>
			and <xref ref="instruction-exercisegroup-vector-geom-dot-prod-vs-vec-add-first-dot-prod">part</xref>.
		</li>

		<li>
			Reflect on the meaning of the <m> + </m> symbol in each
			of <xref ref="instruction-exercisegroup-vector-geom-dot-prod-vs-vec-add-first-add">part</xref>
			and <xref ref="instruction-exercisegroup-vector-geom-dot-prod-vs-vec-add-first-dot-prod">part</xref>.
		</li>

	</ol>
</p></introduction>

<exercise>

	<statement><p>
		<m> \uvec{u} = ( 5, -5) </m>,
		<m> \uvec{v} = (-4,  3) </m>,
		<m> \uvec{w} = ( 2,  2) </m>
	</p></statement>

	<answer><p><ol>

		<li>
			<p><m> \uvec{u} + \uvec{v} = (1,-2) </m></p>
			<p><m>
				\dotprod{(\uvec{u} + \uvec{v})}{\uvec{w}}
				= 1 \cdot 2 + (-2) \cdot 2
				= -2
			</m></p>
		</li>

		<li>
			<p><m> \udotprod{u}{w} = 5 \cdot 2 + (-5) \cdot 2 = 0 </m></p>
			<p><m> \udotprod{v}{w} = -4 \cdot 2 + 3 \cdot 2 = -2 </m></p>
			<p><m> \udotprod{u}{w} + \udotprod{v}{w} = -2 </m></p>
		</li>

	</ol></p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p>
		<m> \uvec{u} = ( 0,5,3) </m>,
		<m> \uvec{v} = ( 3,4,2) </m>,
		<m> \uvec{w} = (-5,4,1) </m>
	</p></statement>

	<answer><p><ol>

		<li>
			<p><m> \uvec{u} + \uvec{v} = (3,9,5) </m></p>
			<p><m>
				\dotprod{(\uvec{u} + \uvec{v})}{\uvec{w}}
				= 3 \cdot (-5) + 9 \cdot 4 + 5 \cdot 1
				= 26
			</m></p>
		</li>

		<li>
			<p><m>
				\udotprod{u}{w}
				= 0 \cdot (-5) + 5 \cdot 4 + 3 \cdot 1
				= 23
			</m></p>
			<p><m>
				\udotprod{v}{w}
				= 3 \cdot (-5) + 4 \cdot 4 + 2 \cdot 1
				= 3
			</m></p>
			<p><m> \udotprod{u}{w} + \udotprod{v}{w} = 26 </m></p>
		</li>

	</ol></p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p>
		<m> \uvec{u} = (-2, 0, 2,-4) </m>,
		<m> \uvec{v} = ( 1,-2, 6,-3) </m>,
		<m> \uvec{w} = (-4,-2, 4,-6) </m>
	</p></statement>

	<answer><p><ol>

		<li>
			<p><m> \uvec{u} + \uvec{v} = (-1,-2,8,-7) </m></p>
			<p><m>
				\dotprod{(\uvec{u} + \uvec{v})}{\uvec{w}}
				= (-1) \cdot (-4) + (-2) \cdot (-2) + 8 \cdot 4 + (-7) \cdot (-6)
				= 82
			</m></p>
		</li>

		<li>
			<p><m>
				\udotprod{u}{w}
				= (-2) \cdot (-4) + 0 \cdot (-2) + 2 \cdot 4 + (-4) \cdot (-6)
				= 40
			</m></p>
			<p><m>
				\udotprod{v}{w}
				= 1 \cdot (-4) + (-2) \cdot (-2) + 6 \cdot 4 + (-3) \cdot (-6)
				= 42
			</m></p>
			<p><m> \udotprod{u}{w} + \udotprod{v}{w} = 82 </m></p></li>

	</ol></p></answer>

</exercise>

</exercisegroup>
